      },
      "message": "fix(motion): name every adaptive level cut by rings; read only ladder planes\n\nEvery arm of machining3d::hsm::plan_level that hands an Adaptive level\nto the Offset rings now goes through one helper, rings_named, which\nwrites \"<why> - Offset rings cut <level> instead\". The text of each note\nis unchanged. If adaptive_passes ever hands back rings without a note\nnaming the level, plan_level adds one.\n\nThe \"radius 5.6 cut by rings, no note\" seen while working #882 was a\nmisread by the test reader, not a planner fallback. The 5.0 level's\nmicrolift down ramp put a vertex on 5.6, and the rotary_adaptive reader\ntook the lifted runs at that height for a level. The reader now reads\nonly the ladder's own planes (top - k * stepdown).\n\nPinned by machining3d::hsm::fallback_tests (a developed level the planner\nrefuses, named by its radius; a planar one, named by its Z; a seam-cut\ndeveloped level) and rotary_adaptive's\na_microlift_plane_is_not_read_as_an_unnamed_ring_level.\n\nFixes #983\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
